It is Friday evening.
I take out my bicycle.
The streets are quite busy.
But now I like riding a bicycle in Mumbai's traffic.
I go to a neighbourhood grocery store.
I need some special Indian spices for the weekend.
I park my bicycle and go straight to the shopkeeper.
"Hello bhaiya," I say.
"Do you have cumin powder and dry mango powder?"
The shopkeeper smiles.
"Yes madam, everything is available," he says.
"How much do you need?"
"Give me one packet of each," I reply.
"And do you also have red chili powder?"
"Yes, I will give you a fresh packet," he says.
He gives me all the spices.
I pay the money and thank him.
I come out of the shop.
I put the spice packets in my bicycle's basket.
Then I ride my bicycle back home.
